Daggers include Sting on the way down through the mines and their
benefit is missile multifire. Knives include crysknife on the way back
up from mines end (if you have a scroll) and they loose as missiles
compared to dagger. Knives do stack but they do not multifire. Many
more of the 3 common types of dagger appear in the mines than the one
common type of knife. This is because of how they appear in the
initial inventories of the monster types that appear in the mines.
Most characters can exit the mines with far more daggers than knives.
For missile combat it's no contest between the two types - Build up a
quiver of daggers soonest and use them constantly to practice the
dagger skill.  Even though a healer only gets a 50-50 chance of firing
1-or-2 daggers per round that's still 150% as good as firing 1 per
round.

For melee orcish dagger matches scalpel all other types beat scalpel
based only on damage not counting weight.  It works to replace your
initial scalpel with the first regular or elven dagger. The gain is
small but not zero. It's not nearly the compelling argument to wield
daggers over knives the way it is with quivering daggers over knives.
It's more a question of how soon you want to gain from the multifire
aspect of daggers. I usually want that as fast as possible so I will
switch to a wielded dagger as soon as possible, then switch back to a
wielded knife class as soon as I reach skilled at dagger.

Once you have a crysknife it's even ambigous if the katana is a
better non-artifact main wield weapon, but crysknife appears later.
Artifacts beat crysknife and not even all of them.  To me all of the
crowning artifacts beat crysknife.  I value artifacts enough that on the
way back up from mines end I will often kill the cross-aligned priest
and convert the altar if I haven't seen any other altars until after
Sokoban.

I also value the luck and holy water to be gained at a converted altar. 
Once those are available it's time to use stacks of darts and move them
up in skills.  Expert multifired darts beat skilled multifired elven
daggers once you no longer risk losing the darts.


